[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Post-OP source pulse parameter state

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Acceptance target: unchanged original regression/misc/alter-vec.cir, original
OP observables, complete original parameter reads/alter/assertions and stock
ngspice full program, without weaker bounds. This is source-parameter state
and reporting support, not new device physics or alteration before a later
analysis. The task's BJT diagnostic copies remain diagnostic and uncounted:
VA is only supported by a selected-DC outer adapter, not general native dynamics.
No approximation or promotion of that profile is authorized by this slice.

Reuse existing generated control metadata, scalar number evaluation, bounded
vector interpreter and prepared source waveform metadata. No additional parser,
legacy runtime or dependency. Retained decisions are in spicesharp-evaluation.md.
Pinned RSpice source guides parameter vector ownership; independently execute
stock ngspice on the unchanged original. Add failing tests, typed pulse alteration,
explicit borrowed parameter slots, post-OP-only admission and complete reporting
failure gating; collect coverage, properties, malformed inputs, mutation and real
StrictDoc evidence. Preserve no-memory-cap campaign policy and all E: artifacts.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONTROL-SOURCE-PULSE-STATE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Typed post-OP pulse parameter vector operation
STATEMENT: >>>
An admitted source pulse alteration shall retain a typed source identity,
parameter kind and seven source-located scalar literals. Only an existing root
independent source with seven explicit pulse parameters may be targeted, after
the sole OP analysis. Alteration before or between analyses, nested alteration,
unknown sources, unsupported parameters and malformed vectors shall refuse.
The operation shall update only owned parameter metadata and preserve all
completed physical result vectors and the original OP request.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: generated control alter production, SourceParameterAlteration,
RequestedControlPreparation and RequestedAnalysis. Verification: SourceAlterTests,
ControlSourceAlterTests and unchanged original alter-vec.cir.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONTROL-SOURCE-PULSE-OWNERSHIP-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Atomic owned source parameter state
STATEMENT: >>>
Pulse parameter reads shall return the currently owned seven-element vector.
The initial parameter arrays and physical input arrays borrowed from callers
shall never be mutated. An alteration shall validate its target, cardinality
and finite scalar values before publishing replacement state. Failed reporting
shall publish no successful result or partial external effect. Pulse amplitudes
retain source units and the remaining five entries retain seconds; no additional
physical timing defaults or later simulation semantics shall be inferred.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: negative/alias/ownership tests and reproducible FsCheck properties;
evidence/source-pulse-alter.json. Numerical OP agreement is distinct from command
execution, assertion success and future-analysis source alteration support.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CORPUS-TERMINAL-ASSERTION-GATE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Terminal failure prevents whole-program agreement
STATEMENT: >>>
Every attempted required terminal reporting region shall inspect both diagnostics
and exit status. A failed assertion or reporting error shall prevent whole-program
native agreement even when individual numerical analyses agree. Ordered and
single-analysis reporting shall share this failure gate; unattempted reporting
shall not be represented as executed.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: RequestedCorpus. Verification: authored negative pulse assertion
fixture, preserving its numerical agreement and explicit program failure.
<<<
